What does this program print?
```c
#include <stdio.h>

int total;

void add(int amt) {
    int val;
    val = amt * 2;
    total += val;
}

int main(void) {
    total = 1;
    add(3);
    add(4);
    printf("%d\n", total);
    return 0;
}
```

Given:
```c
int g_x;

int change(int amt) {
    int val;
    val = g_x;
    g_x += amt;
    return val;
}
```
`main` sets `g_x = 10;` and then runs `result = change(10);`. What is the value of `g_x` afterward?
